 "plain_language_summary": "This is an outlook, not a forecast: NOAA's Climate Prediction Center gives a 50% chance of above normal rain for Dec-Feb and a 50% chance of above normal rain for Jan-Mar, with a 33% chance of above normal temperature for Dec-Feb (about 33% is what any category gets in an average year). Mc Clure (Exchequer) holds 498,942 acre-feet (115% of CDEC's average for 13 Nov). The Drought Monitor week of 2026-11-10 shows abnormally dry (20% of the county at the D0 level or worse), and NOAA's drought outlook through 31 Jan shows no drought. Alfalfa kept this field covered through most winters, so there is no typical bare window to report (only 1 of 7 winters had 14 or more bare days). Under the outlook scenario, the current rotation needs about 4.2 acre-feet per acre in 2027 (range 4.2-4.3), little changed from a normal year.",
